note <Two kernel gaps compile/node.tree found (2026-10-05), each held by a program that failed before>

# Ported from form-named-type.ts by hand (item 0557).
#   1. A form named `type`. The kernel reads `like type` as its universe, so every task answering the form failed as `kernel: type
#      mismatch`. check/elaborate.ts `kindsApart` now renames such a form on the kernel's own copy.
#   2. A construction that leaves a `need false` field out. The surface checker allows it, the kernel's constructor takes every field. The
#      kernel now declines such a construction, as it declines an unresolved name.
# The third check is reached in the original only when the second holds, and here it asks the same.

load ../support/compiling
  find compile-text
  find compile-choice
  find compile-outcome

load @term/base/text
  find contains, name text-contains

task build
  take source, like text
  like compile-outcome

  back compile-text(source, make(compile-choice, bind(file, <kernel.tree>), bind(stdlib, <node>), bind(library, true), bind(lean, true)))

host optional, <form shape\n  case open\n    link free\n      like boolean\n      need false\n  case closed\n\ntask open-shape\n  like shape\n\n  back make open\n>

test <a task answering a form named type builds>
  want hold, build(<form type\n  mark tag, name kind\n  case number\n  case named\n    link name, like text\n\ntask number-type\n  like type\n\n  back make number\n>)/ok

test <a construction leaving a need false field out builds>
  want hold, build(optional)/ok

test <and the field is left out of what it builds>
  host out, build(optional)
  want hold, out/ok
  want hold, text-contains(out/emitted, <\{ form: "open" \}>)
